  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#script-nomodule-example\r\n\r\n```\r\n<script type=​\"module\" src=​\"app.mjs\"></script>\r\n<script nomodule src=​\"classic-app-bundle.js\"></script>\r\n```\r\n\r\n`type=module` has defer behaviour by default whereas classic scripts are blocking.\r\n\r\nShould the `defer` attribute be added to the `nomodule` example to make the scripts equivalent from an execution point of view and also reinforce the defer behaviour of modules?\r\n\r\n",
